# Keymap

Platform shortcuts are **declarative**. Do not add ad-hoc `keydown` listeners for shell/K chrome.

## Wire a control

1. Put `data-keymap-id="<id>"` on the focusable/clickable element (`KEYMAP_ID_ATTR` from `@/lib/keymap`).
2. Add a binding in the app’s `keymap.yaml` (core: `apps/core/keymap.yaml`).
3. Add `labelKey` strings to `locale/en.po` + `fa.po`; run `kaizengo gen-types <app>` for `template.pot`.

```yaml
# apps/core/keymap.yaml
- id: search_focus
  action: element:k-search   # clicks/focuses [data-keymap-id="k-search"]
  keys: alt+f
  labelKey: keymap.shell.search_focus
  scope: global
  hint: true
  inForm: true               # optional — fire while focus is in inputs
```

## Action kinds

| Action | Effect |
|--------|--------|
| `element:<id>` | Activate `[data-keymap-id="<id>"]` (click / focus+select for inputs) |
| `custom:<name>` | Handler from `useKeymapAction(name, fn)` |
| `shell.*` / `nav.<app>` | Built-ins in `lib/keymap/actions.ts` |

## K chrome ids (core)

| Id | Control |
|----|---------|
| `k-search` | Search input |
| `k-search-filter` | Filter button |
| `k-search-group` | Group button |
| `k-page-prev` / `k-page-next` | Pagination |
| `form-save` | KForm submit |

Reuse these ids — do not invent parallel shortcut systems in views. Prefer `labelKey` with underscores (`keymap.shell.search_focus`); hyphens truncate in pot codegen.
